---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import { GraduationCap, Code, Globe, Building2, MapPin, FileCheck, Server, UserCheck } from 'lucide-astro';
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';

import govProgramsImg from '../../assets/government-programs.png';
---

<PageLayout
  title="For Indian Government & PSUs — AI Resource Exploration"
  description="CAGE-IN gives GSI and NCMM project teams AI-augmented mineral prospectivity at mission cadence — India-resident IP, Results-as-a-Service, defensible under GFR Rule 194."
>

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════
       Section 1 — Hero
  ══════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="bg-geo-slate text-white py-16 md:py-24">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 text-center" data-reveal>
      <p class="text-geo-gold text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.3em] mb-5">For Indian Government &amp; PSUs</p>
      <h1 class="font-display text-4xl sm:text-5xl md:text-6xl text-white leading-[1.08] mb-6">
        NCMM cadence. AI-augmented prospectivity. India-sovereign from day one.
      </h1>
      <p class="text-slate-300 text-base md:text-lg leading-relaxed max-w-prose mx-auto mb-8">
        The Geological Survey of India faces a structural capacity gap: 1,200 exploration projects by FY 2030–31, a legacy data backlog that spans decades, and a manual re-interpretation cycle that runs six to twelve months per licence area. AI Resource Exploration (AiRE) has built the only India-registered, India-IP-held, production-deployed AI prospectivity engine that compresses that cycle to weeks — delivering ranked target portfolios from your own legacy data, on India-resident infrastructure, with capacity transfer built in.
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-center gap-4">
        <a
          href="/contact?intent=gsi-pilot"
          class="w-full sm:w-auto px-8 py-3.5 rounded bg-geo-gold text-white font-semibold text-sm uppercase tracking-wider hover:bg-amber-500 transition-colors text-center"
        >
          Request a GSI Pilot Brief →
        </a>
        <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-4 py-2 rounded border border-geo-gold/50 text-geo-gold text-[10px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em]">
          Available under GFR Rule 194 nomination
        </span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════
       Section 2 — The NCMM capacity gap
  ══════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="py-12 md:py-20 bg-geo-deep">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="text-center mb-10" data-reveal>
        <p class="text-geo-gold text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.25em] mb-3">The Capacity Gap</p>
        <h2 class="font-display text-3xl md:text-5xl text-white mb-6 leading-tight">
          NCMM requires 1,200 exploration projects by FY 2030–31.<br class="hidden md:block" />
          Manual workflows cannot deliver that cadence.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <!-- 4-stat strip -->
      <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-6 mb-10" data-reveal>
        {[
          { num: '₹34,300 cr', label: 'NCMM outlay over 7 years' },
          { num: '1,200',      label: 'Target projects by FY 2030–31' },
          { num: '195',        label: 'Projects ongoing FY 2024–25' },
          { num: '227',        label: 'Projects planned FY 2025–26' },
        ].map(({ num, label }) => (
          <div class="text-center">
            <p class="font-display text-4xl md:text-5xl text-geo-gold leading-none mb-2">{num}</p>
            <p class="text-slate-400 text-xs uppercase tracking-wider leading-snug">{label}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>

      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto" data-reveal>
        <p class="text-slate-300 text-base leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Even at peak field-team utilisation, GSI's traditional reconnaissance-to-prospecting cycle cannot ingest the legacy aerogeophysical, geochemical, and remote-sensing datasets at the rate NCMM requires. Each licence area demands a 3–5-person specialist team six to twelve months to manually re-interpret — a throughput ceiling that no hiring programme alone can break through.
        </p>
        <p class="text-white font-semibold text-base">
          AI-augmented prospectivity is no longer optional.
        </p>
        <p class="text-slate-400 text-sm mt-2">
          The policy direction was confirmed by the IndiaAI – GSI Hackathon on Mineral Targeting (launched March 2025, winners announced November 2025). The question now is whether GSI commissions a production-ready engine or waits for academic prototypes to catch up.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════
       Section 3 — Why CAGE-IN (4-archetype grid)
  ══════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="py-12 md:py-20 bg-geo-slate">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="text-center mb-10" data-reveal>
        <p class="text-geo-gold text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.25em] mb-3">Why CAGE-IN, not the alternatives</p>
        <h2 class="font-display text-3xl md:text-5xl text-white mb-4 leading-tight">
          Four challenger paths. Four reasons CAGE-IN wins.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6" data-reveal>

        <!-- Hackathon prototypes -->
        <div class="card-dark rounded-xl p-6">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-geo-primary/20 text-geo-secondary flex items-center justify-center mb-4">
            <GraduationCap size={20} />
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-display text-lg text-white font-semibold mb-2 leading-snug">Academic hackathon prototypes</h3>
          <p class="text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Excellent research, not production. The IndiaAI–GSI Hackathon (November 2025) validated the demand and produced strong academic outputs — the IIT(ISM) Dhanbad CricSM AI team being the standout. These are research deliverables requiring further productisation. CAGE-IN is the production-ready option that eliminates GSI's risk of funding that gap.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- FOSS stacks -->
        <div class="card-dark rounded-xl p-6">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-geo-primary/20 text-geo-secondary flex items-center justify-center mb-4">
            <Code size={20} />
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-display text-lg text-white font-semibold mb-2 leading-snug">Open-source / FOSS stacks</h3>
          <p class="text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Generic machine learning on satellite data — without a proprietary reasoning flowsheet, without deposit-model calibration, and without a geological consistency layer. Outputs land unranked or shallow-ranked. CAGE-IN's three-engine architecture (Method A WLC + Method B Random Forest + Ensemble Fusion) is not replicable by assembling off-the-shelf components.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- International AI vendors -->
        <div class="card-dark rounded-xl p-6">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-geo-primary/20 text-geo-secondary flex items-center justify-center mb-4">
            <Globe size={20} />
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-display text-lg text-white font-semibold mb-2 leading-snug">International AI vendors</h3>
          <p class="text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Foreign jurisdiction, foreign IP, foreign data processing. Each of these introduces MeitY data-localisation friction and Aatmanirbhar Bharat misalignment that will surface at the file-note stage. AiRE is Indian-registered with India-held IP — the award is unambiguously sovereign.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- In-house GoI build -->
        <div class="card-dark rounded-xl p-6">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-geo-primary/20 text-geo-secondary flex items-center justify-center mb-4">
            <Building2 size={20} />
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-display text-lg text-white font-semibold mb-2 leading-snug">In-house GoI build</h3>
          <p class="text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Costs years of development time and competes directly with NCMM cadence requirements. Buying a productised, production-deployed solution is the established GovTech pattern — it is why CERT-In contracts empanelled auditors, why UIDAI licensed biometric SDK vendors, and why dozens of Ministries contract specialist consultancies for mission-critical AI work.
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════
       Section 4 — Sovereign by design
  ══════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="py-12 md:py-20 bg-geo-deep">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="text-center mb-10" data-reveal>
        <p class="text-geo-gold text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.25em] mb-3">Sovereign by Design</p>
        <h2 class="font-display text-3xl md:text-5xl text-white mb-4 leading-tight">Built in India. For India.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-4" data-reveal>

        <div class="card-dark rounded-xl p-5 flex flex-col items-start gap-3">
          <div class="w-9 h-9 rounded-lg bg-geo-primary/20 text-geo-secondary flex items-center justify-center">
            <MapPin size={18} />
          </div>
          <p class="text-slate-300 text-sm leading-snug">
            India-incorporated<br />
            <span class="text-slate-500 text-xs">CIN U74999TG2017PTC115998, est. 2017</span>
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="card-dark rounded-xl p-5 flex flex-col items-start gap-3">
          <div class="w-9 h-9 rounded-lg bg-geo-primary/20 text-geo-secondary flex items-center justify-center">
            <FileCheck size={18} />
          </div>
          <p class="text-slate-300 text-sm leading-snug">
            India-held IP<br />
            <span class="text-slate-500 text-xs">Wholly owned by AiRE</span>
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="card-dark rounded-xl p-5 flex flex-col items-start gap-3">
          <div class="w-9 h-9 rounded-lg bg-geo-primary/20 text-geo-secondary flex items-center justify-center">
            <Server size={18} />
          </div>
          <p class="text-slate-300 text-sm leading-snug">
            India-resident processing<br />
            <span class="text-slate-500 text-xs">No data leaves India</span>
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="card-dark rounded-xl p-5 flex flex-col items-start gap-3">
          <div class="w-9 h-9 rounded-lg bg-geo-primary/20 text-geo-secondary flex items-center justify-center">
            <UserCheck size={18} />
          </div>
          <p class="text-slate-300 text-sm leading-snug">
            Founder-led Indian national<br />
            <span class="text-slate-500 text-xs">Dr. Amit Tripathi, Principal</span>
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════
       Section 5 — Living Methodology callout
  ══════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="py-12 md:py-16 bg-geo-slate">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8" data-reveal>
      <div class="bg-geo-gold/8 border border-geo-gold/30 border-l-4 border-l-geo-gold rounded p-7">
        <p class="text-geo-gold text-[10px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.25em] mb-3">Living Methodology</p>
        <p class="font-display italic text-white text-lg md:text-xl leading-snug mb-4">
          AI-backed fluid software — CAGE-IN's reasoning evolves as the geoscience literature evolves. The model you commission today is the model you keep, kept current.
        </p>
        <p class="text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Static AI competitors — hackathon prototypes, frozen ML stacks, international vendor snapshots — cannot make this claim. A model trained at a point in time cannot absorb the deposit-model refinements in next year's peer-reviewed literature. CAGE-IN is engineered to.
        </p>
        <a
          href="/technologies/cage-in#living-methodology"
          class="text-geo-gold text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider hover:text-amber-400 transition-colors"
        >
          See how CAGE-IN stays current →
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════
       Section 6 — Procurement options
  ══════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="py-12 md:py-20 bg-geo-deep">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="text-center mb-10" data-reveal>
        <p class="text-geo-gold text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.25em] mb-3">Procurement Frame</p>
        <h2 class="font-display text-3xl md:text-5xl text-white mb-4 leading-tight">Three routes. All defensible.</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-400 text-base leading-relaxed max-w-prose mx-auto">
          CAGE-IN is delivered as a consultancy-and-other-services engagement. The governing rule is GFR 2017 Rule 194 — but three independent procurement frames stack to give the file robustness against challenge.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6" data-reveal>

        <!-- GFR Rule 194 -->
        <div class="card-dark rounded-2xl p-8 flex flex-col">
          <p class="text-geo-gold text-[10px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.25em] mb-3">Primary route</p>
          <h3 class="font-display text-xl text-white font-semibold mb-4 leading-snug">
            GFR Rule 194 — Single Source by Nomination
          </h3>
          <p class="text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed flex-1">
            Rule 194(iii) permits single-source consultant selection where the assignment involves "proprietary techniques" or "unique expertise." Both limbs are independently satisfied: CAGE-IN is a documented proprietary technology held by an Indian company, and AiRE's 30+ years of field practice across 60+ projects in 20+ countries establishes unique expertise. Lower documentary burden than Rule 166; administered by the user Ministry without manufacturer-attestation infrastructure.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- PPP-MII Class-I -->
        <div class="card-dark rounded-2xl p-8 flex flex-col">
          <p class="text-geo-gold text-[10px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.25em] mb-3">Companion route</p>
          <h3 class="font-display text-xl text-white font-semibold mb-4 leading-snug">
            PPP-MII Class-I Local Supplier
          </h3>
          <p class="text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed flex-1">
            Under the Public Procurement (Preference to Make in India) Order 2017, AiRE qualifies as a Class-I local supplier — Indian incorporation, India-developed IP, and local-content threshold above 50 percent. Citing PPP-MII alongside Rule 194 advances the Aatmanirbhar Bharat narrative and pre-handles any procurement-preference challenge. The PPP-MII grievance portal exists precisely to enforce this preference.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Startup India -->
        <div class="card-dark rounded-2xl p-8 flex flex-col">
          <p class="text-geo-gold text-[10px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.25em] mb-3">Easements</p>
          <h3 class="font-display text-xl text-white font-semibold mb-4 leading-snug">
            Startup India Procurement Easements
          </h3>
          <p class="text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed flex-1">
            Once DPIIT Startup India recognition is secured (process underway), AiRE qualifies for exemption from prior-experience and prior-turnover criteria on GeM and CPPP. This removes the single most common technical disqualification applied to emerging technology vendors in government procurement, and is specifically designed for the situation where a newer company holds demonstrably superior technology.
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════
       Section 7 — Capacity building
  ══════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="py-12 md:py-20 bg-geo-slate">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-14 items-center">

        <!-- Left: content -->
        <div data-reveal>
          <p class="text-geo-gold text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.25em] mb-3">Capacity Building</p>
          <h2 class="font-display text-3xl md:text-5xl text-white mb-6 leading-tight">
            Buy a capability. Build a team.
          </h2>
          <p class="text-slate-300 leading-relaxed mb-6">
            Every government-scale CAGE-IN engagement includes an embedded capacity-building module — because dependency on a vendor is a CAG audit risk, and institutional capability transfer is not.
          </p>
          <ul class="text-slate-300 space-y-4 text-sm">
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="text-geo-gold mt-0.5 shrink-0">→</span>
              <span>GSI geoscientists trained on the CAGE-IN platform, plugin operation, and the deposit-model framework — not just the interface, but the geological reasoning behind each evidence family.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="text-geo-gold mt-0.5 shrink-0">→</span>
              <span>Methodology updates delivered as the peer-reviewed literature evolves — your team inherits each improvement as it ships, not on a separate contract cycle.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="text-geo-gold mt-0.5 shrink-0">→</span>
              <span>Refresher training cycles included at each scale-up phase — ensuring competency is maintained as new AOIs, new commodities, and new deposit types enter the pipeline.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="text-geo-gold mt-0.5 shrink-0">→</span>
              <span>Interpretation workshops on confidence scores, conflict maps, and the geological meaning of disagreement zones — the features most frequently cited in CAG performance reviews as evidence of genuine knowledge transfer.</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- Right: image -->
        <div data-reveal>
          <Image
            src={govProgramsImg}
            alt="Government programs and capacity building"
            width={600}
            class="rounded-2xl shadow-xl border border-white/10 w-full object-cover"
          />
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════
       Section 8 — Results-as-a-Service
  ══════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="py-12 md:py-20 bg-geo-deep">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="text-center mb-10" data-reveal>
        <p class="text-geo-gold text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.25em] mb-3">Commercial Model</p>
        <h2 class="font-display text-3xl md:text-5xl text-white mb-4 leading-tight">
          Results-as-a-Service — payment only on acceptance.
        </h2>
        <p class="text-slate-400 text-base leading-relaxed max-w-prose mx-auto">
          The contract is engineered so that the Internal Finance Wing's concurrence is straightforward. The exchequer pays for accepted deliverables, benchmarked against GSI's own internal cost to execute the equivalent task.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-5 gap-3" data-reveal>

        <div class="card-dark rounded-xl p-5">
          <p class="text-geo-gold text-[10px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] mb-2">Payment Trigger</p>
          <p class="text-slate-300 text-sm leading-relaxed">Acceptance of ranked-target deliverable against pre-defined technical specification. No payment for effort that does not produce GSI-approved outputs.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card-dark rounded-xl p-5">
          <p class="text-geo-gold text-[10px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] mb-2">Unit of Pricing</p>
          <p class="text-slate-300 text-sm leading-relaxed">Per AOI (km²) and per accepted target above confidence threshold — each unit price benchmarked against GSI's own internal cost. The same-task comparator IFW concurrence relies on most.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card-dark rounded-xl p-5">
          <p class="text-geo-gold text-[10px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] mb-2">Phase Structure</p>
          <p class="text-slate-300 text-sm leading-relaxed">Phase 1 Pilot (1–2 AOIs) with GSI acceptance review, followed by Phase 2 Scale-up. Built-in performance gate before commitment to the full project pipeline.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card-dark rounded-xl p-5">
          <p class="text-geo-gold text-[10px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] mb-2">Liquidated Damages</p>
          <p class="text-slate-300 text-sm leading-relaxed">Standard GoI consultancy LD clauses on missed milestones. Standard risk transfer to vendor — same terms as every other GoI consultancy contract.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card-dark rounded-xl p-5">
          <p class="text-geo-gold text-[10px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] mb-2">Termination</p>
          <p class="text-slate-300 text-sm leading-relaxed">30-day notice, pro-rata payment for accepted deliverables only. Exit option preserved for GSI at all times with no lock-in beyond accepted work.</p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════
       Section 9 — CTA banner
  ══════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="py-14 md:py-24 bg-geo-slate text-white relative overflow-hidden border-t border-white/5">
    <div class="absolute inset-0 opacity-[0.03]" style="background-image: repeating-linear-gradient(45deg, #fff 0, #fff 1px, transparent 0, transparent 50%); background-size: 30px 30px;"></div>
    <div class="relative z-10 max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 text-center" data-reveal>
      <p class="text-geo-gold text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.3em] mb-4">Free Consultation</p>
      <h2 class="font-display text-3xl md:text-5xl text-white mb-6 leading-tight">
        Ready to brief a sponsoring division?
      </h2>
      <p class="text-slate-300 text-base md:text-lg leading-relaxed max-w-prose mx-auto mb-8">
        A 30-minute call with Dr. Amit Tripathi covers your AOI, your NCMM project pipeline, and which procurement route best fits your division's existing delegation of financial powers — at no cost and no commitment.
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-center gap-4 mb-5">
        <a
          href="/contact?intent=gsi-pilot"
          class="w-full sm:w-auto px-8 py-3.5 rounded bg-geo-gold text-white font-semibold text-sm uppercase tracking-wider hover:bg-amber-500 transition-colors text-center"
        >
          Request a GSI Pilot Brief →
        </a>
        <a
          href="/contact"
          class="w-full sm:w-auto px-8 py-3.5 rounded border border-white/20 text-white/80 font-medium text-sm hover:bg-white/10 transition-colors text-center"
        >
          Email a brief instead
        </a>
      </div>
      <p class="text-slate-500 text-[10px] uppercase tracking-widest">No commitments · Results-as-a-Service · India-resident processing</p>
    </div>
  </section>

</PageLayout>
